{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_46c9544a2141",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9810,
      "mechanism": "The failure shows o_mosi emitting wrong bits when r_cmd_state >= 3'h5 (command sent, awaiting response). In state 3'h5, ll_fifo_rd is asserted only if (r_use_fifo && r_fifo_wr). Adding && r_have_resp prevents starting a FIFO read before the first response token is confirmed, avoiding premature FIFO data on o_mosi. Cited source line 9810 is the r_use_fifo gate controlling ll_fifo_rd in state 3'h5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_3a11c0f77d92",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9810,
      "mechanism": "Same gating location as patch_46c9544a2141 but qualifying with r_fifo_wr instead of r_have_resp. In state 3'h5, ll_fifo_rd should only start for write commands using FIFO. This patch mirrors the original intent (r_fifo_wr indicates a write) and prevents spurious FIFO reads for read commands, which would drive o_mosi with 0xff fill bytes early. Source line 9810 is the exact r_use_fifo condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6278fcd13e60",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9715,
      "mechanism": "In state 3'h5, r_use_fifo is used to choose the next state (3'h6 vs 3'h7). The failure indicates the response-state machine may advance incorrectly when r_use_fifo is asserted without a confirmed response. Adding && r_use_fifo ensures the second_rsp_state assignment to SDSPI_RSP_GETTOKEN only occurs for FIFO writes, stabilizing the rsp_state progression that ultimately controls ll_cmd_stb and o_mosi timing. Source line 9715 is the r_cmd_state == 3'h5 condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_b9cc3bb103f8",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 8360,
      "mechanism": "pre_cmd_state is the enable for the entire command-state machine (the block at line 9127). The failure window starts at cycle 484124 where o_mosi toggles unexpectedly, suggesting the command sequencer ran a cycle early/late. Qualifying the top-level entry with && pre_cmd_state ensures the state machine only advances when the low-level interface is idle, aligning the first command byte emission. Source line 8360 is the if (!ll_cmd_stb) block reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_03cf2d2c8b87",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 8623,
      "mechanism": "Inside the command sequencer, pre_cmd_state gates each step (line 9127). The failure shows an extra/missing o_mosi transition at the boundary where ll_cmd_stb asserts. Changing the guard to (pre_cmd_state && !ll_cmd_stb) prevents the state machine from advancing in the same cycle ll_cmd_stb becomes asserted, avoiding a one-cycle shift in command-byte emission on o_mosi. Source line 8623 is the pre_cmd_state assignment."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2e6db5d7770e",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9010,
      "mechanism": "The first command-byte step (r_cmd_state == 3'h0) emits the MSB of the command. The failure's first mismatch at cycle 484124 aligns with this byte. Adding && !ll_cmd_stb prevents the step from firing if the low-level transmitter is not yet idle, ensuring the first MOSI bit coincides with ll_idle. Source line 9010 is the r_cmd_state == 3'h0 branch."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_97989b13811d",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9778,
      "mechanism": "At line 9778 (inside state 3'h5), r_have_resp is used to enable ll_fifo_wr. The failure shows spurious FIFO write data on o_mosi. Changing to (r_have_resp && r_use_fifo) ensures the write-channel only opens for FIFO write commands after a response token, preventing early 0xFE start-token emission. Source line 9778 is the ll_fifo_wr assignment."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_70dca1511670",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 10047,
      "mechanism": "In state 3'h6 (FIFO read completion), the sequencer waits for ll_fifo_rd_complete. The failure shows an extra 0xff on o_mosi after the read should have ended. Qualifying the state with && r_fifo_wr ensures this state is only active for write commands (where 3'h6 is a write-completion state), preventing read-command leakage into the write-completion path that would keep ll_cmd_stb asserted and drive o_mosi. Source line 10047 is the r_cmd_state == 3'h6 branch."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The trace mismatch starts at cycle 484124 on o_mosi with a pattern of bit inversions, indicating the SPI command sequencer is one cycle off or emitting FIFO fill bytes prematurely. The highest-leverage fixes gate the command-state machine entry (patch_b9cc3bb103f8, patch_03cf2d2c8b87), the first byte emission (patch_2e6db5d7770e), the FIFO-read start condition (patch_46c9544a2141, patch_3a11c0f77d92), the response-token-aware state selection (patch_6278fcd13e60), the FIFO-write start (patch_97989b13811d), and the write-completion state (patch_70dca1511670). All target lines lie in the single always @(posedge i_clk) block under if (pre_cmd_state) in sdspi.v, so each patch is a localized condition guard with minimal scope."
}
